      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! I found the answer.\n\nAccording to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by **never holding it there in the first place**. Instead:\n\n1. **A local secrets loader** reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. **The key is injected only into the child process environment** of the spawned Ingest agent, immediately before that process starts\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** with the credential\n\nThis design prevents a compromised or misbehaving Hub process from leaking the API key simply by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only in the short-lived child process that actually needs it to call the Anthropic API. The same scoping model applies to the Query agent process as well.",
      "input_tokens": 4305,
      "output_tokens": 185
    }
